From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:25:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: Add Allwinner A733 IOMMU driver

The A733 has two IOMMU instances: IOMMU0 serves USB, CSI, ISP and the
video encoder, IOMMU1 the video decoder, the display engine, the
deinterlacer, G2D and EINK. sun50i-iommu cannot drive them: ENABLE and
TTB sit at 0x14 and 0x20, each master has a 0x200-byte block of its own
with its own bypass bit, and page table entries carry 34-bit addresses.

The user manual has no register description. The offsets follow
Allwinner's BSP driver, and what the driver needs for translation was
read back on hardware; registers known from the BSP alone are marked
"(BSP)" in the source.

There is one IOMMU device and one group per instance. The identity
domain is the per-master bypass bit, which is also the reset state. TLB
maintenance is a full flush, the global TLB first and then the micro TLB
of each translating master, because the done bit of the range
invalidation does not drop while the video engine is idle. A master's
MBUS port gate, an optional "masterN" clock, is held while the master
has a user. Every fault interrupt is cleared and the masters involved
are reset, which can include a master that faulted earlier, as L1PG_INT
and L2PG_INT can keep its bit. A fault is reported, except an L1 or L2
prefetch fault, which only flushes the TLBs. An early resume callback
programs the block again from the driver's state; nothing is saved.

The probe sets ENABLE, the interrupt enable and TTB to 0, their reset
value, and warns when an earlier boot stage left them otherwise. It
does not touch the per-master blocks, whose port gates are off then.

Not covered: runtime PM, and the permission and L2 fault paths, which
have not been exercised.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; both instances bind,
register their interrupts and read back their version register (0x16),
no instance reports translation left on by the boot chain, and with no
master attached translation stays disabled.

Assisted-by: LLM
